### Rewriting the radical as a rational power

$\begin{align}
g(x)&=\sqrt[3]{x^4}
\\\\
&=x^{^{\Large\frac{4}{3}}}
\end{align}$

### Differentiating using the power rule

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}g'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(x^{^{\Large\frac{4}{3}}}\right)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{4}{3}x^{^{\Large\frac{4}{3}-1}}\qquad\gray{\text{The power rule}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac43x^{^{\Large\frac{1}{3}}}
\end{align}$
